  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196100: Bounded PostgreSQL transaction state and ErrorResponse

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The database provider exports `pg_query_state` in addition to the existing
success-only `pg_query`. It reads through exactly one final ReadyForQuery,
validates every bounded frame, permits a structurally valid ErrorResponse, and
returns two metadata bytes: success/error kind and PostgreSQL transaction
state (`I`, `T`, or `E`). A malformed ErrorResponse, message after an error
other than another error or ReadyForQuery, premature ReadyForQuery, overflow,
or missing final state fails closed.

The independent-memory linker now permits a manifest to declare a fixed-size
copy-out buffer. Response bytes continue to use the provider result length;
the transaction metadata copy is exactly two bytes and is still checked
against the consumer capacity.

## Executable evidence

The released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification authenticates with
SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS and runs `BEGIN`, an intentional division-by-zero, and
`ROLLBACK` on the same affine TLS channel. The compiled `.kotoba` consumer
requires the exact state sequence `T`, `E`, `I`. Parser tests accept a bounded
field-coded ErrorResponse and reject a missing final terminator.

This closes transaction state recovery and bounded error framing, but does not
yet expose selected SQLSTATE/message fields as a typed application record.
Prepared statements, bind parameters, cancellation, pooling, credential and
certificate rotation, version/cloud matrices, and soak remain open."}]
